From 60e15d68166784ce41d11aa4a280ad74d0087ca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:44:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 108/109] fix(classifier): keep load errors valid UTF-8, and
 name at least one refused dir

Review round 4 of B204.

Round 3's printable() cut echoed values at 120 bytes, mid-character, and
passed through bytes that are not UTF-8 (a raw directory name). The
refusal reason then became invalid UTF-8, the /load handler's dump()
threw (type_error.316), and the client got no JSON error body at all.
printable() now escapes every byte that does not start a well-formed
UTF-8 sequence (and control characters) as \xNN, and cuts only on a
character boundary. ModelLoader::write_load_error also dumps with
error_handler_t::replace, as network_beacon.cpp and websocket_server.cpp
already do, so a byte that slips through cannot cost the body.

A single refusal line over the 2 KiB budget used to become "and 1 more"
with no directory or reason. The first refused directory is now always
listed, with its path cut to 512 bytes and its reason to 1 KiB, and room
is kept for the "and N more" line so the whole list stays within 2 KiB.

require_layout now escapes the model name and directory it quotes. A
crash or watchdog reset during the image-route probe reads "the engine was
reset during the probe" instead of quoting the watchdog's promise of an
automatic reload, which a refused load does not do.

Tests: test_classifier_layout checks a labels_file cut inside a two-byte
character, a directory name with bytes 0xff 0xfe, a refusal line over
2 KiB and an escaped model name, on all three engines.
server_image_classify.py adds test_520a/b (the /load body stays valid
JSON with the reason for both cases), test_519f (the reset outcome) and,
for row Z, test_519e (a 2xx probe answer refuses the load) with the
fake's new FAKE_PROBE_OK.

